# Repo-root .dockerignore — apps' Dockerfiles are built with the repo
# ROOT as context (`docker build -f apps/<app>/Dockerfile .`) so the
# libs/* go.mod replace targets resolve inside the context.
# Each Dockerfile COPYs only the dirs it needs (libs/hostkit, libs/jinja
# for node-host-agent, + its own app dir); this list just keeps the
# context small and reproducible.
.git/
.github/
.moon/
**/bin/
**/dist/
**/node_modules/
**/*.test
**/coverage.out
# Source-tree files no Dockerfile consumes: go build ignores _test.go
# and testdata/ (and none of these images run tests), *.md ships in the
# build stage only via whole-dir COPYs, go.work must stay OUT so builds
# run in plain module mode like CI, and mise/.golangci are dev-only.
**/*_test.go
**/testdata/
**/*.md
go.work*
mise.toml
.golangci.yml
# Gitignored build outputs that must not leak into the build context
# (a stale apps/node-host-agent/agent is ~47MB). These sit beside the
# **/bin/ dirs already excluded above.
apps/node-host-agent/agent
apps/node-automation-controller/manager
apps/webhook-dispatcher/dispatcher
